      "math_academy_id": "q-77542",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "The measure of one angle in a triangle is four times the measure of another angle, and the measure of the third angle is ${85}^{∘}.$ What is the measure of the smallest angle?",
      "worked_solution": "Let $x$ be the measure of the first angle. Then the measure of the second angle is $4x.$\n\nThe sum of the measures of the interior angles must be ${180}^{∘}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+4x+{85}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 5x+{85}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 5x & ={95}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={19}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nHence, the measure of the smallest angle is ${19}^{∘}.$",
